Section name: Application to Database Systems
Excerpt:
In Example 1, we highlighted the application of 𝜀-nets as dataset summaries for range queries , where the goal is to compress potentially very large datasets to a small subset that contains at least one tuple from any possible (axis-parallel) range query. The 𝜀-net can then facilitate AQP by quickly identifying a tuple in the set that satisfies a query range. In the following, we briefly outline some other applications of 𝜀-nets,𝜀-samples, and geometric hitting set in database systems and beyond. 𝜀-samples are foundational to Approximate Query Processing (AQP) because they provide small yet statistically representative subsets of the data. By ensuring that the selectivity of every query range deviates by at most 𝜀from that on the full data, they en- able consistent accuracy guarantees for aggregate functions such as COUNT, SUM, and AVG. Modern systems like VerdictDB [ 70] implement hiera

